# Reawakening OS - core system.
# Only what the machine needs to boot, connect and stay healthy.
linux-image-amd64
live-boot
live-config
live-config-systemd
systemd
systemd-sysv
systemd-zram-generator
udev
dbus
# The polkit daemon. Only the client libraries were installed before, so every
# privileged D-Bus action was refused: NetworkManager answered the "connect to
# this Wi-Fi network" request with 'Not authorized to control networking'
# whatever the password, and udisks2 could not mount a drive. The default policy
# asks for an administrator password, so this image also ships a rule that lets
# the desktop account (group netdev) do those things without a prompt.
polkitd
sudo
network-manager
# Wi-Fi scanning and WPA/WPA2/WPA3 association. NetworkManager calls
# wpa_supplicant for the actual association; without it every scan comes back
# empty and "no networks found" is the only possible result.
wpasupplicant
iw
bluez
rfkill
pipewire
pipewire-pulse
# ALSA applications (including most native games) reach PipeWire through this.
pipewire-alsa
# Per-machine mixer profiles (UCM): without them many laptop codecs come up
# with the wrong output selected, or muted.
alsa-ucm-conf
alsa-utils
wireplumber
libspa-0.2-bluetooth
wireless-regdb
ca-certificates
# `ip` and `ss`: refurb-cockpit prints the addresses another computer can use
# and refurb-diag reports the interface state. NetworkManager does not pull
# iproute2 in with --no-install-recommends, so it has to be named.
iproute2
# Real-time scheduling for PipeWire. Without rtkit every audio operation logs
# RTKit errors and runs at normal priority; on the 2 GB target machine that is
# audible as dropouts when the CPU is busy. D-Bus activated, no idle process.
rtkit
curl
apt
dpkg
locales
tzdata
console-setup
keyboard-configuration
nano
less
btop
initramfs-tools
# The disk installer (refurb-install). These are the tools it runs: unpack the
# live squashfs, partition and format the target, and put GRUB on it. The
# installed system keeps them, so `update-grub` and a later grub-install work
# without installing anything first. The *-bin packages are used instead of the
# grub-pc/grub-efi meta packages because their postinst asks for a device and
# cannot run during a rootless image build.
squashfs-tools
dosfstools
e2fsprogs
fdisk
parted
grub-common
grub2-common
grub-pc-bin
grub-efi-amd64-bin
os-prober
